WEBVTT - Module 5: Hero Command Center

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.000
All right, welcome to the Hero Command Center!

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.500
This is your playbook for becoming a true community hero.

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:13.500
That number is the estimated deaths from burns worldwide every single year. The threat is absolutely real!

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.500
To defeat an enemy, you've got to know it. Fire is fast, dark, hot, and deadly.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
And this is exactly why we're here — because every community needs heroes, and that hero can be you!

6
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.500
Here in the Command Center, we're going to equip you with the tools you need to protect everyone.

7
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
A true hero has a balanced strategy. Think of it like having two shields: Prevention and Reaction.

8
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:46.500
Let's start with your first shield: Prevention. This is all about stopping a fire before it even starts.

9
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.500
A hero knows the terrain, so you've got to watch out for common fire hazards at home.

10
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:03.000
But your primary mission: creating a home fire escape plan. It's crucial! This five-step plan turns your home into a safe zone.

11
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.500
You've got to memorize and practice it!

12
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.500
Okay, now for your second shield: Reaction. This is what you do when an emergency is already happening.

13
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:20.500
Just remember the acronym R-A-C-E (Rescue, Alarm, Contain, Extinguish/Evacuate).

14
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.500
What if your clothes catch on fire? That's a critical emergency, and there's a specific protocol for it:

15
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.500
Do NOT run! Just STOP, DROP, and ROLL!

16
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.500
This simple action smothers the flames and can save your life.

17
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.500
A hero's duty often extends to helping the injured, so you have to know basic first aid.

18
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.500
The leading preventable cause of death from trauma is bleeding. Just remember your ABCs!

19
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.000
And that's it — your training is complete! You have the playbook, but there is nothing without action.

20
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.000
A student, Gabriel, used this very training to save his neighbor's home. It proves you can do it too!

21
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:04.500
This training makes you a leader, but it's your actions that are going to make you a hero.

22
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.500
So the real question is: when that alarm sounds, how will you answer the call?
